 Ethiopia The National Library of Ethiopia today holds more than 800 items in its manuscript collection, chiefly in Ge'ez, Amharic, and Arabic. The UNESCO and EMML projects together microfilmed 165 Christian and secular codices from this instiution's holdings. Collection Eastern Christian Country Ethiopia City Addis Ababa Repository National Archives and Library of Ethiopia Project Codes EMML; UNESCO Project Numbers EMML 7384-7505 (nonsequential); UNESCO 2-1 - 2-106 Type Digital/Microform Objects Preserved 174 Active Catalog Records 174 Digital Surrogates 174 Microfilm Reels 70 Date Preserved 1969-1970, 1980 HMML Reading Room (sample record) https://www.vhmml.org/readingRoom/view/500906 HMML Authority File https://haf.vhmml.org/organization/297697130592 Languages Ge'ez, \n            \n            Amharic, \n            \n            Arabic Bibliography Imperial Ethiopian Government Antiquities Administration, Catalogue of the Ethiopian Manuscripts in the National Library of Ethiopia (Addis Ababa, 1969/1970); Ministry of Education and Fine Arts, Catalogue of Manuscripts Microfilmed by the UNESCO Mobile Microfilm Unit in Addis Ababa and Gojjam Province (Addis Ababa, 1970) Preservation Status Complete Cataloging Status In progress Legacy Catalog Yes Collections News Cataloging progress ; Cataloging progress Get the latest news direct to your mailbox Email Magazine You can unsubscribe at any time. Collections Western European Manuscripts Eastern Christian Manuscripts Islamic Manuscripts Buddhist & Hindu Manuscripts Malta Manuscripts Special Collections Art & Photographs Vööbus Syriac Manuscripts Archival Collections at HMML Repository List Research Digital Tools Fellowships Visiting Scholars Image Reproduction Services Initiatives Malta Study Center Programs Public Programs Scholarly Programs Stories Latest Stories All Stories About History Global Operations Staff Board of Directors News & Media Resources Publications FAQ Contact Support Giving Societies Donor Advised 